<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liao dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Khitan Liao, Liao</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Liao dynasty was a state founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khitans">Khitans</a> that ruled northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a> from the tenth to the early twelfth century. It was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a>'s principal northern rival, and the Treaty of Chanyuan in 1005 obliged the Song to make annual payments to the Liao. The Liao was overthrown by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchens">Jurchen</a> Jin in the 1120s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty.jpg" alt="Liao dynasty" width="320" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Liao_circuits.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
